PR Contributor Declaration (checker landed, rollout pending):

The action, the reusable workflow and this repo's own template are in. What
remains is turning it on across the org, in this order -- reversing steps 3 and
4 fails contributors who faithfully used their own repo's template, because a
template change only affects NEW pull requests while every already-open one
keeps its old body.

1. add the standard consumer caller to this repo:
   .github/workflows/contributor-declaration.yml, exactly the README snippet.
   It must reference
   ecmwf/ci-infrastructure/.github/workflows/check-pr-declaration.yml@main, so
   pr-declaration-dogfood.yml is not a substitute: it runs on `pull_request`,
   right for developing the checker, wrong for enforcement.

2. measure the blast radius before requiring anything anywhere. Run the checker
   over every open pull request in the org
