Two gaps that need a merge-time check, both documented in the action's
description. Neither is closable at pull_request_target time:

- merge queues. A pull_request_target workflow never runs on `merge_group`, so a
  repo that enables a merge queue would have entries wait for a check that never
  arrives, time out (60 min default) and be dequeued -- every PR in that repo
  unmergeable. Extend the gate BEFORE any repo turns a queue on: parse the PR
  number out of refs/heads/gh-readonly-queue/<base>/pr-<N>-<sha> and read the
  body with `body-source: api`, since there is no pull_request payload there.

- a description edited with GITHUB_TOKEN does not start a new workflow run, so
  an automation calling `gh pr edit --body ''` leaves the earlier green result
  standing. Wants either the merge_group leg above or a post-merge audit on
  `push: main` that re-reads the merged PR's body and opens an issue on
  mismatch.

HPC:

- per-run HPC job paths. hpc-jobs/<artifact>.out and staging/<artifact>/deps
  are keyed on the artifact name alone, so two runs of the same artifact share
  them (the output is filtered by job id, but a concurrent run can still
  overwrite it). Keep reattach keyed on the SLURM job name; split output and
  deps paths per run, and decide what a reattaching run tails.

- -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH in the HPC recipes is inert, and is a trap the day the
  environment stops covering for it. jobscript.py exports CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH
  colon-joined (plan_remote_prefixes returns ":".join(...)), which is correct for
  an ENVIRONMENT variable. But ecflow's four recipes
  (.ci/hpc/build-{gnu,intel,aocc,nvidia}.sh) then pass
  -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH="$CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH", and a -D CACHE variable is a
  SEMICOLON-separated list -- so the colon-joined string arrives as one path that
  does not exist.

  Today the env var rescues it; with an empty env var (a no-deps build) the
  -D path alone fails with "Could not find ... ecbuild".

  Fix either way: drop the -D from the recipes and let the env var do the work, or
  emit the value semicolon-joined for -D use. Do not leave both halves disagreeing.

- ecflow's hpc-atos-gnu leg is red on a runtime libstdc++ mismatch, unrelated to
  the nvidia memory kill. ctest's python tests fail with
  "ImportError: /lib64/libstdc++.so.6: version `GLIBCXX_3.4.32' not found
  (required by .../libs/pyext/python3/ecflow.so)": the extension is built with the
  gcc/15.2.0 module but resolves the SYSTEM libstdc++ (8.5.0) when imported.
  -DCMAKE_INSTALL_RPATH_USE_LINK_PATH=ON does not help -- it governs the INSTALL
  tree, and ctest runs out of the build tree. Wants the module's libstdc++ on the
  runtime path for the test step (LD_LIBRARY_PATH, or a build-tree RPATH).

